args: opentide --json doctor --help
exit: 0

━━━ stdout
Check the installation, the workspace and its integrations

Each check prints a status, what it found and, when something needs doing,
the command that fixes it. Credentials are reported as set or unset, never
printed. With --live, each tenant whose credentials are set is also reached:
the sign-in a deploy makes, then one read-only request, nothing written.
Exits 1 when any check fails; warnings alone exit 0.

Usage: opentide doctor [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --offline
          Skip the network checks (PyPI release, proxy reachability)

      --live
          Reach each tenant whose credentials are set: sign in, then one read-only request

      --help
          Print help

Examples:
  $ opentide doctor
  $ opentide doctor --offline
  $ opentide doctor --live
  $ opentide --json doctor

━━━ stderr · empty
